      <h1>Zanzibar Airport Transfer Guide</h1>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p>Abeid Amani Karume International Airport (ZNZ) receives daily flights from Nairobi, Dar es Salaam, Istanbul, and many seasonal charter operators. Getting from the airport to your Zanzibar accommodation is the first step of your island experience, and pre-booking a fixed-price transfer is the most reliable, stress-free option.</p>

      <h2>Transfer Options by Zone</h2>

      <h3>Stone Town (Mji Mkubwa)</h3>
      <p>The historic capital is the most popular destination, located just 5–7 km from the airport. <strong>Travel time:</strong> 15–25 minutes. <strong>Spice &amp; Sail published rate:</strong> $18 private sedan (1–3 passengers) / $35 private van (4–6 passengers). Unofficial airport touts typically ask $35–50.</p>
      <p>Why pre-book? Stone Town's taxi touts outside the arrivals hall often quote inflated prices ($50–80) to unsuspecting visitors. A pre-arranged transfer through your hotel, a licensed operator, or WhatsApp booking ensures you pay the agreed rate, have a driver waiting with a name sign, and avoid negotiation stress after a long flight.</p>
      <p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> If you must take an official airport taxi, insist on the meter or agree on the price <strong>before</strong> entering the vehicle. The official airport desk can also arrange a trusted driver.</p>

      <h3>Nungwi (North Zanzibar)</h3>
      <p>Zanzibar's northernmost village is a popular beach resort area. <strong>Travel time:</strong> 60–80 minutes. <strong>Spice &amp; Sail published rate:</strong> $45 private sedan (1–3 passengers) / $50 private van (4–6 passengers). Typical airport street taxi asks $60–80.</p>
      <p>The route follows the modern paved north highway. Peak tourist arrival windows can add 15 minutes of town traffic. Pre-booking guarantees a dedicated air-conditioned private vehicle with flight monitoring.</p>
      <p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Many visitors combine the transfer with a spice farm visit along the way. Confirm with the concierge on WhatsApp.</p>

      <h3>Paje / Jambiani (Southeast Zanzibar)</h3>
      <p>The southeast coast's famous kitesurfing and beach villages. <strong>Travel time:</strong> 50–70 minutes. <strong>Spice &amp; Sail published rate:</strong> $45 private sedan (1–3 passengers) / $50 private van (4–6 passengers). Typical street rate $70–90.</p>
      <p>The route crosses the island through picturesque palm corridors. The road condition is fully tarmac.</p>
      <p><strong>Pro tip:</strong> Many kitesurfing visitors prefer a pre-booked transfer that waits at the airport regardless of arrival delays. Confirm your driver's mobile number via WhatsApp before arrival so you can coordinate exact pickup location.</p>

      <h3>Kendwa (North Zanzibar)</h3>
      <p>Neighboring Nungwi's beach resort area, famous for non-tidal swimming. <strong>Travel time:</strong> 60–80 minutes. <strong>Spice &amp; Sail published rate:</strong> $45 private sedan (1–3 passengers) / $50 private van (4–6 passengers). Street taxi rate $65–80.</p>

      <h3>Other Zones</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Jambiani:</strong> Similar to Paje, 50–70 minutes, $45 private sedan / $50 private van.</li>
        <li><strong>Kizimkazi / Michamvi / southern coast:</strong> 60–90 minutes, $50 private sedan / $50 private van.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Transfer Types & Booking</h2>

      <h3>Private Vehicle</h3>
      <p>The most convenient option: your party has the vehicle to yourselves. Ideal for families, groups, or travelers with luggage. Prices above are per vehicle (1–3 passengers in a sedan, 4–6 in a van). Book via WhatsApp (+255 672 450 934), email (reservations@spiceandsail.com), or through your hotel's concierge.</p>

      <h3>Shared Shuttle</h3>
      <p>More economical for solo travelers or couples. You share the vehicle with other arriving passengers heading to the same general zone. Wait times may be 30–60 minutes as the shuttle fills. Cost: approximately $25–40 per person for Stone Town and $35–50 per person for Nungwi/Paje, subject to availability.</p>

      <h3>Hotel Arrival Transfer</h3>
      <p>Many Zanzibar hotels and lodges offer complimentary or paid arrival transfers for guests. Check with your accommodation before booking separately. If your hotel charges $30–50 for a private transfer, compare with independent operators—you may find better value elsewhere.</p>

      <h2>Cost-Saving Tips</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Book in advance:</strong> Pre-booking via WhatsApp or email often secures the fixed price; walk-up fares are typically 20–30% higher.</li>
        <li><strong>Share a vehicle:</strong> If you're solo or as a couple, consider a shared shuttle to cut costs by 50% or more.</li>
        <li><strong>Avoid airport touts:</strong> Never accept a ride from someone approaching you inside the terminal. Follow the signs to the official taxi rank or your pre-arranged driver.</li>
        <li><strong>Confirm the price:</strong> Always confirm the total price includes waiting time (typically 30–60 minutes free) and meet-and-greet (driver with name sign).</li>
        <li><strong>Check what's included:</strong> Some prices include meet-and-greet, flight tracking (for delayed flights), and one small bottle of water. Clarify before departure.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Emergency & Contingencies</h2>
      <p>Flight delays are common. Choose a transfer provider that offers <strong>flight tracking</strong>—they'll adjust pickup time at no extra charge. If your flight is more than 2 hours late, most operators will either wait free of charge or offer to reschedule without penalty. Keep your driver's WhatsApp number saved, and send a message if you're running late.</p>
      <p>In the rare event no pre-arranged driver appears, proceed to the official airport taxi stand and insist on the metered rate or a quoted price before entering the vehicle. The airport information desk can also assist in calling a trusted operator.</p>
      <p>Zanzibar airport transfers are straightforward when you plan ahead. By booking a fixed-price transfer through a licensed operator, you'll start your island holiday on the right note—without haggling, surprises, or overpaying.</p>
